{"duration_api_ms": 52564, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "session_id": "ca75fc9a-2197-4ede-9563-e568a49c8a68", "total_cost_usd": 0.015130619999999996, "usage": {"input_tokens": 36, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 30700, "cache_read_input_tokens": 584352, "output_tokens": 10892, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 3433}, "server_tool_use": {"web_search_requests": 0, "web_fetch_requests": 0}, "service_tier": "standard", "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 30700}, "inference_geo": "global", "iterations": [{"input_tokens": 2, "output_tokens": 855, "cache_read_input_tokens": 43256, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 358, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 358, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0}, "type": "message"}], "speed": "standard", "fallback_credit": null}, "modelUsage": {"claude-haiku-5-5": {"inputTokens": 36, "outputTokens": 10892, "cacheReadInputTokens": 584352, "cacheCreationInputTokens": 30700, "webSearchRequests": 0, "costUSD": 0.015130619999999996, "contextWindow": 1000000, "maxOutputTokens": 128000, "thinkingTokens": 3433, "canonicalModel": "claude-haiku-5-5", "provider": "firstParty", "costBasis": "list"}}, "permission_denials": [], "terminal_reason": "completed", "fast_mode_state": "off", "fast_mode_disabled_reason": "sdk_opt_in_required", "subagent_stats": {"spawned": 0, "requested": {"background": 0, "foreground": 0, "unset": 0}, "started_in_background": 0, "max_depth": 0, "spawned_by_subagents": 0, "completed": 0, "failed": 0, "killed": {"parent": 0, "user": 0, "system": 0}, "refused": {"depth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 19, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "`on_setattr` hooks can now be generator functions, and the spec's check passes: `tests/test_compat.py` and `tests/test_setattr.py` give 52 passed and 1 xfail. The xfail (`test_slotted_confused`) is already marked as expected-to-fail in the repo. The full `tests/` suite also passes (1399 passed, 7 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\nWhat changed, by file:\n\n- **`src/attr/_compat.py`**: added `_IS_GENERATOR_RESULTS` and `_lazy_is_generator`. The check is cached per function, and unhashable callables get the uncached answer.\n- **`src/attr/_make.py`**: the generated `__setattr__` handles generator hooks as the spec describes. It also wraps the `attrib` docstring with the 26.2.0 `versionchanged` note.\n- **`src/attr/_next_gen.py`**: `define` and `field` docstrings have the new sentences and `versionchanged` notes.\n- **`src/attr/setters.py`**: `pipe` has the warning that generator functions aren't allowed. Its behaviour is unchanged.\n- **`src/attrs/__init__.pyi`**: `_OnSetAttrType` also accepts generator-returning callables.\n- **`docs/examples.md`**: added the \"Running Custom Code Before/After Setting Attributes\" section with the doctest example.\n\nChoices I made where the spec left room:\n\n- The spec says `_ClassBuilder._make_own_setattr`, but that method doesn't exist here. The `__setattr__` generation lives in `add_setattr`, so I changed that.\n- A generator that yields nothing at all will let `StopIteration` escape from `__setattr__`. The spec doesn't cover this case, so I left it alone.\n\nChecks I ran beyond the spec:\n\n- The `docs/examples.md` example gives the expected output when run directly.\n- Running stdlib `doctest` on `docs/examples.md` reports 63 failures, all in other sections because of missing imports under that runner. None involve the new section, so I didn't pursue it further.\n- `ruff check` reports one `RUF063` on `_compat.py:35`, which is in code I didn't touch.\n\nI haven't committed anything. `SPEC.md` is still untracked.", "ttft_ms": 1328, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 64351, "uuid": "733a2307-7e7e-4071-844f-41665d7bfdd3", "ttft_stream_ms": 1144, "time_to_request_ms": 314, "first_content_frame_ms": 1144, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 0}
